            <title><![CDATA[Updates to Full Disk Access in macOS (165 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=p6zjojqw</link>
            <guid>49937631</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 19:37:01 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=p6zjojqw">https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=p6zjojqw</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49937631">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><section id="main" role="main">
					
					
										
					<article id="article-p6zjojqw">
						<section>
								
																																									<p><img src="https://developer.apple.com/assets/elements/icons/full-disk-access/full-disk-access-256x256_2x.png" width="0" height="0" alt="Updates to Full Disk Access in macOS" data-hires="false">
									</p>
																								
																	
								
								
								<div>
									<p>October 2, 2026</p>
																			<div><p>We give developers powerful APIs to build incredible capabilities into their apps for Apple products, backed by a set of controls designed to protect users’ private data. Full Disk Access largely sidesteps these controls in order to allow backup apps to function properly on the Mac. Some developers are using Full Disk Access in ways that could put users at risk, exposing everything on their systems—including files, mail, messages, and even browsing history—without users’ full knowledge and understanding. For communication apps, this can also compromise the privacy of the people users are communicating with.</p><p>Going forward, we will introduce additional controls to ensure that users who genuinely wish to grant an app this extraordinary level of access can only do so with very explicit user action. Addressing this is critical. As AI agents become increasingly capable and autonomous, the risks associated with this level of access will grow substantially. We are committed to ensuring users clearly understand these risks before granting such access, so they can make informed decisions about their own data and privacy.</p></div>

																	</div>

																
															</section>


					</article>
									</section></div>]]></description>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Muse Gadgets (170 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://gadgets.muse.ai</link>
            <guid>49937504</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 19:26:54 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://gadgets.muse.ai">https://gadgets.muse.ai</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49937504">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div id="main-content"><div aria-labelledby="home-title"><p>Muse gadgets are open source devices you build yourself. Program an off-the-shelf ESP32 board or set up a Raspberry Pi with our SDKs, then connect Muse to your displays, buttons, sensors, actuators, and whatever else you’ve got lying on your workbench.</p><figure><img alt="Muse gadgets: a Waveshare round AMOLED, an M5Stack StickS3, Muse&nbsp;Home&nbsp;Link, a Raspberry Pi and a Seeed reTerminal e-ink display" loading="lazy" width="1520" height="320" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/muse-gadgets-lineup.png?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></figure></div><div><div><div id="build-your-own" aria-labelledby="build-your-own-title" data-gadgets-hero-module="build-your-own"><p><span>01 / ON YOUR HARDWARE</span></p><div><div><h2 id="build-your-own-title">Make your own</h2><div><p>We <a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk">open sourced</a> the code you need to make a Muse gadget. It’s built by hackers, for hackers, just for fun. Side effects of tinkering may include bricked boards, voided warranties, brownouts, or bankruptcies. Proceed at your own risk!</p><p>Get started by grabbing an <a href="https://gadgets.muse.ai/settings/sdk-tokens">SDK token</a> and one of our featured <a href="#esp32-muse-devices">project&nbsp;ideas</a>. Then tinker and customize to your heart’s delight. Or build support for an entirely new board if that’s more your thing.</p></div></div><div><div><h3><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/tree/main/esp32" aria-label="ESP32 Device SDK" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>ESP32 Device SDK</span></a></h3><p><small>Connect your ESP32 board to Muse through our open source SDK. Throw in a screen to show images, add audio in and out, or wire up other sensors.</small></p></div><div><h3><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/tree/main/linux" aria-label="Linux Device SDK" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Linux Device SDK</span></a></h3><p><small>Turn that spare Raspberry Pi or Linux box into a Muse gadget. Hack in your own commands to let Muse handle sysadmin chores or your Home Assistant setup.</small></p></div></div></div></div><div><section id="discord" aria-labelledby="community-title"><p><span>03 / BUILD TOGETHER</span></p><p>Meet other hackers who are building and customizing Muse gadgets in our community Discord. Get inspired, support each other, and share what you make.</p><p data-discord-online="true">68 members online now</p><a href="https://discord.gg/3bhjCkZdd6" data-gadgets-join-discord="true"><span>Join Discord</span></a></section><section id="github" aria-labelledby="source-title"><p><span>04 / OPEN IT UP</span></p><h2 id="source-title">Source</h2><p>Explore the source code for our device SDKs and firmware. Use it as a starting point for your projects and contribute your improvements back to the community.</p><p>The device SDKs and firmware are open source under the Apache 2.0 license and provided as-is, without warranty.</p><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk"><span>Muse Gadgets on GitHub</span></a></section></div></div><article aria-labelledby="product-title" data-gadgets-hero-module="home-link"></article></div><section id="esp32-muse-devices" aria-labelledby="esp32-muse-devices-title"><p><span>05 / MUSE GADGET EXAMPLES</span></p><div role="region" aria-label="Project Ideas carousel" data-can-scroll-next="true"><ul id="esp32-muse-devices-carousel" tabindex="0"><li><div><figure role="img" aria-label="Raspberry Pi 5"></figure><p><span><strong>Raspberry Pi 5</strong><small>Give Muse a way to work with Home Assistant and other popular Linux applications.</small><span><a href="https://www.walmart.com/ip/Raspberry-Pi-5-SC1160-8GB-RAM-Single-Board-Computer/5820957894" aria-label="Buy Raspberry Pi 5" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/tree/main/linux" aria-label="Source for Raspberry Pi 5" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure><picture><source media="(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)" srcset="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/waveshare-happy-esp32.webp"><img alt="Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C" loading="lazy" width="516" height="387" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/waveshare-happy-esp32-poster.webp?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></picture></figure><p><span><strong>Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C</strong><small>A round 1.75″ AMOLED touch screen with push-to-talk, a speaker and mic, and a battery.</small><span><a href="https://www.waveshare.com/esp32-s3-touch-amoled-1.75c.htm" aria-label="Buy Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.muse-waveshare-s3-175c" aria-label="Source for Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure><img alt="Wireframe drawing of an HDMI stick" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="741" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/tv-stick-wireframe-light.png?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"><img alt="Wireframe drawing of an HDMI stick" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="741" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/tv-stick-wireframe-dark.png?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></figure><p><strong>Muse on your TV</strong><small>A stick that plugs into your TV’s HDMI port so you can ask Muse to put things up on the big screen.</small><span>Coming soon</span></p></div></li><li><div><figure><img alt="Seeed reTerminal E1002" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/seeed-e1002-briefing-photo.webp?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></figure><p><span><strong>Seeed reTerminal E1002</strong><small>Give your Muse a color e-ink display. Muse can show a morning briefing, reminders, shopping list, or anything else you think of.</small><span><a href="https://www.seeedstudio.com/reTerminal-E1002-p-6533.html" aria-label="Buy Seeed reTerminal E1002" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.reterminal-e1001" aria-label="Source for Seeed reTerminal E1002" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure><img alt="M5Stack StickS3" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/m5stack-sticks3-user-photo.webp?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></figure><p><span><strong>M5Stack StickS3</strong><small>A pocket-size M5Stack device with a color screen showing Muse’s status and a front button.</small><span><a href="https://shop.m5stack.com/products/m5sticks3-esp32s3-mini-iot-dev-kit" aria-label="Buy M5Stack StickS3" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.muse-m5stack-sticks3" aria-label="Source for M5Stack StickS3" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure><img alt="AiPi Lite" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="900" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" src="https://gadgets.muse.ai/gadgets/aipi-lite-stock.webp?dpl=dpl_AFsruwC4637UYEJRBPBmDS54G8or"></figure><p><span><strong>AiPi Lite</strong><small>A tiny desk buddy for Muse. Press a button to talk, and Muse answers out loud and shows pictures on the color screen.</small><span><a href="https://aipi.com/products/aipi-lite" aria-label="Buy AiPi Lite" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.muse-aipi" aria-label="Source for AiPi Lite" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure role="img" aria-label="ideaspark ESP32 with 1.9″ display"></figure><p><span><strong>ideaspark ESP32 with 1.9″ display</strong><small>Give Muse a little status screen. See what Muse is up to at a glance, and let it draw pictures on the 1.9″ color display.</small><span><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D6QXC813" aria-label="Buy ideaspark ESP32 with 1.9″ display" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.ideaspark" aria-label="Source for ideaspark ESP32 with 1.9″ display" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li><li><div><figure role="img" aria-label="Home Assistant Voice Preview Edition"></figure><p><span><strong>Home Assistant Voice Preview Edition</strong><small>Talk to Muse with push-to-talk on its speaker and mic, and see Muse’s status on its LED ring.</small><span><a href="https://www.home-assistant.io/voice-pe/" aria-label="Buy Home Assistant Voice Preview Edition" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Buy</span> </a><a href="https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk/blob/main/esp32/devices/sdkconfig.home-assistant-voice" aria-label="Source for Home Assistant Voice Preview Edition" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Source</span> </a></span></span></p></div></li></ul></div><p>Devices shown here are made and sold by other companies, and Meta doesn’t endorse or warrant them.<!-- --> <!-- -->Names and logos belong to their owners.</p></section></div></div>]]></description>
